<!--
  Plots of land without roads, each one walled in by roads (#43). One country, AAA, a square from 1°W to 3°E and
  1°S to 1°N, with a hole that is the country BBB: a square from 0.73°E to 0.75°E and 0.05°S to 0.03°S, 2.2 km a
  side, which no road reaches. Every road is secondary (60 km/h): one along the equator from 0° to 2°E, and four
  loops off it, each road of a loop meeting the equator's at its own node. Each corner of a loop away from the
  equator has a stub of road 1.1 km outwards, so the builder keeps the corner: it collapses a chain of nodes no other
  road meets into one straight edge.

  On the equator 0.1° is 11.12 km (the engine's sphere has a radius of 6371.0088 km): 0.222 h of travel from the
  origin, the equator's west end. The land up to 1 km from a road is in the ring with it, so what of a plot is
  further from its roads is the plot less 1 km on each side; the engine takes it in when it is under 200 km².

    A  0.6°E – 0.65°E, 0° – 0.05°N: 5.6 km a side, 3.6 × 3.6 km = 13 km² away from the roads, a small plot. Its
       roads are reached from 1.33 h (0.6°E on the equator) to 1.56 h (its north-east corner): in the 2 h ring.
    D  0.7°E – 0.78°E, 0.08°S – 0°: 8.9 km a side, 6.9 × 6.9 km = 47 km² away from the roads, BBB in it, 3.3 km from
       each road. A small plot, reached from 1.56 h (0.7°E) to 1.91 h (its south-east corner): in the 2 h ring.
    B  1°E – 1.3°E, 0° – 0.3°N: 33.4 km a side, 31.4 × 31.4 km = 984 km² away from the roads, a large plot. Its
       roads are reached from 2.22 h (1°E) to 3.56 h (its north-east corner, either way round): all in 4 h.
    C  1.3°E – 1.35°E, 0.05°S – 0°: as small as A. Its roads are reached from 2.89 h (1.3°E) to 3.11 h (its south-east
       corner); its west side is reached within 3 h but for its last 0.1 km, its south and east sides after 3 h
       (1.35°E on the equator at 3.002 h): the roads of 3 h leave it open to the east, those of 4 h wall it in.

      0.3°N                               +------------------+
                                          |                  |
                                          |        B         |
     0.05°N              +--+             |                  |
                         |A |             |                  |
         0°  0 . . . . . +--+ +----+ . . .+------------------+-+ . . . . . 2°E
                              | D  |                         |C|
     0.05°S                   | [] |                         +-+
     0.08°S                   +----+
                        0.6°E 0.7°E   1°E                 1.3°E 1.35°E
-->
